{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774715,"nonce":"otsT+K+dtfPcT7UuY9YEt4F6kKI=","title":"Dogfood follow-ups: 6 fixes (log-tail noise, silent status, artifacts index, run_as_root workspace, boot-time App PEM, App-config runbook)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #25 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `batch/dogfood-followups` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-17T19:26:26Z · Merged: 2026-07-18T05:19:27Z\n\nA batch of dogfood-surfaced fixes, one commit per ticket, all verified by `cargo test` (176 pass, 13 live-cluster ignored).\n\n| git-bug | Commit | Fix |\n|---------|--------|-----|\n| `c653742` | `fix(log-tail)` | Stop WARN-spamming while a step Pod is `PodInitializing`/`ContainerCreating`; log those at debug, keep WARN for real errors (matches the benign *reasons*, not the generic `waiting to start:` prefix, so `ImagePullBackOff`/`CrashLoopBackOff` still warn). |\n| `ba921db` | `fix(forge)` | `drain_forge_statuses` dropped the `set_status` `Err` silently. Now log it, `record_outbox_failure`, and dead-letter the **message** after `MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS` (mirrors scheduler poison handling, ADR-0047) — never dead-letters the run. New test drives a rejecting forge and asserts retry-then-dead-letter. |\n| `98ea804` | `fix(executor-k8s)` | Artifacts uploaded but never indexed. The harvest + annotation patch run in the egress native sidecar's settle leg, which doesn't gate the Pod phase, so `Succeeded` was observed before the annotation landed → scheduler read `[]` once and never again. `poll()` now withholds **only** the `Succeeded` verdict while the egress sidecar is still running (deterministic, no sleeps). |\n| `b04697f` | `fix(executor-k8s)` | `run_as_root` (or any non-`65532` uid) step couldn't write `/workspace`: the CAS feed `tar` resets the tree to `65532:65532 0755`, clobbering the `fsGroup` group-writability. Restore `g+rwX` + setgid on dirs after the feed. Rejected adding `CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE` (would bypass ADR-0039 governed grants). |\n| `245a99c` | `feat(forge)` | Boot-time GitHub App PEM via `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM` / `..._FILE`, overriding the DB-stored `_forge` credential — bootstrap-free / GitOps, survives DB recreate. Helm: `secrets.githubAppPem`. **Caveat:** connection/installation registration is separate state, still seeded via reseed/webhook. |\n| `70aa42e` | `docs(deploy)` | Runbook section: the App must subscribe to events **and** grant `statuses:write` — both fail silently otherwise. |\n\n- The two executor fixes share `crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs`, so they're one commit.\n- Coverage: new unit/integration tests for `ba921db` (dead-letter path + `FakeForge::failing_status`), the `c653742` classifier, and `245a99c` config parsing. The two k8s-runtime fixes (`98ea804`, `b04697f`) are additionally covered by the crate's ignored live-cluster tests; happy to drive them on colima if wanted.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}